' RWin32.inc in a RapidR program: RapidR's own built-ins stay RapidR's
' (SLEEP here, in seconds, on every system), RAPIDQ.INC's numbers are built
' in (MB_ICONERROR) and True is RapidR's -1. The classic program gets the
' DLL's Sleep: rwin32_builtins_classic.bas.
$INCLUDE "RWin32.inc"
SLEEP 0
PRINT "RapidR's SLEEP"; MB_ICONERROR; True; WM_CLOSE
